>> COMPONENT OVERVIEW <<

TYPE - COMPONENT        RESPONSIBILITY

C - Main                create a GameApp object and run it

C - GameApp             runs app and controls app flow

C - GameFramework       create game of given GameType
E - GameType            list of playable games

I - Game	            generic game interface
I - Move                generic move interface
E - GameResult          list of game results (works separate from server)
E - GameEndReason       list of game ending types (works separate from server)
C - TicTacToeModel	    rules & game state
C - TicTacToeView	    display game/board
C - TicTacToeController	bridge between Model and View
C - TicTacToeMove       game specific move constructor

C - Client	            handles connection to server
E - MessageType         list of general server message types
E - MessageSubtype      list of specific server message types
I - ServerListener      deals with incoming server messages
C - ServerMessageParser cut up server messages into type, subtype & fields --> Map<String, String>
C - ServerMessage       constructor + getters

I - Player              generic player interface
C - localPlayer         create an instance of a local player
C - Ai                  decide what move to make
C - OnlinePlayer        create an instance of a player on the server

C - Ui                  General ui layer
C - MainMenu            display main menu options & get user input
C - GameMenu            display game menu options & get user input



>> APP FLOW <<

1. start app
Main --> GameApp

2. main menu
GameApp --> MainMenu --> "play"

3. choose game
GameApp --> GameMenu --> TIC_TAC_TOE (GameType)

4. framework creates game
GameApp --> GameFramework --> TicTacToeModel

5. MVC system
TicTacToeModel <-->    TicTacToeController    <--> TicTacToeView
check moves/   <-->  get response from Model  <--> update with new move
game state           tell View to update

6. making moves
terminal (ui) input --> controller --> Model.doMove(...) --> AI.pickMove() --> Model isValidMove() --> controller --> View.printBoard(...)
(human makes move)                                      (bot makes move)

> localPlayer --> move input from (G)ui (terminal for now)
> Ai --> move input from calculation based on current board state
> onlinePlayer --> move input from server message



>> ONLINE PLAY FLOW <<
own move
terminal (ui) input --> controller --> model --> client --> server

opponent move
server --> client --> ServerListener --> ServerMessageParser --> ServerMessage --> controller --> model --> view




>> SERVER MESSAGE FLOW <<

server --message--> Client --> ServerMessageParser --> ServerMessage --> other classes



>> LOCAL GAME FLOW <<

MainMenu --"play"--> GameMenu --"tic-tac-toe" + "local"--> GameFactory --> TicTacToeModel --[player makes move]-->

    TicTacToeController --> TicTacToeMove(5 or col 2, row 2) --> TicTacToeModel --update--> TicTacToeView
      check move &                     do move                    tell View to
      game state                                                 update with move